Fillets: a rounding's end past the spine's end where one contact ran off
its face (mitcad#236).

A rounding along a top face's edge with a wall, where the top narrows to
nothing at the spine's end and the wall runs on past that vertex (into a
face tangent to it): the top's contact runs off the top across its edge
with a sloped face before the end. PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine walks the
piece from there past the spine's end on the top's tangent plane and
gives that side up (ChFi3d_Purge: no face, its point where the contact
left the top). The corner then dropped that piece and failed at the end
of the piece before it ("Failed to find edge"). The files' bodies run the
blend on past the vertex, cut along the given-up side by the sloped face
and at its end by the face beyond the wall.

- The given-up piece continues the elementary blend before it where it
  lies on that blend's surface: it takes that surface, its p-curves
  projected onto it (ChFi3d_ExtensionOnNeighbourSurface), and the blend
  is one face up to where the corner cuts it.
- PerformOneCorner keeps such a piece where both its ends at the corner
  lie on edges and the piece before it does not end on edges.
- PerformIntersectionAtEnd takes, as the face of a given-up side, the
  face that side had before (where its contact ran off), and, where an
  elementary blend whose side was given up does not cross an edge
  between the faces at the end within its bounds, bounds it wider along
  its spine (by its own extent, short of a whole period) and takes the
  crossing on that edge.

Upstream: new.
